    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved all date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), keeping the three affected outputs internally consistent.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the single source of truth for derived owner fields:\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 returns the fiscal year as an int. A date in July or later belongs to the next calendar year's fiscal year (named by the year it *ends*, the Australian convention consistent with the rest of the app), earlier dates to the current year's. So 2026-09-04 \u2192 FY 2027.\n- Added `fiscalYear(Owner)` \u2014 returns `FY<YY>` (e.g. `FY27`) from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (which `BuildOwner` already rolls forward and stores). Null when the date is absent.\n- **Membership number** now uses the fiscal year for its `M<YY>` segment (e.g. `NSW-16E6609E-M27`) instead of the raw calendar year.\n- **Tenure** (the +3 membership-points rule) now triggers on **one or more elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearOf(now) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) >= 1`) rather than a 365-day window.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from it at build time):\n- Added the `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via a `@Mapping`.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreReturnsFiscalYear` passes (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`), and the audit log confirms the consistency: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` for a 2026-09-04 registration \u2192 FY27.",
